│  Welcome to your ultimate guide for an unforgettable trip to Madrid, Spain!                                   │
│                                                                                                               │
│  As a local expert, I'm thrilled to share with you the best of Madrid, tailored to your interests in art,     │
│  history, food, and culture. Given your travel dates of February 14th to 16th, 2026, you've chosen a great    │
│  time to visit Madrid, with mild weather perfect for sightseeing.                                             │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Weather Forecast**                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                               │
│  Madrid's weather in February is generally pleasant, with highs around 12°C (54°F) and lows at 4°C (39°F).    │
│  Don't forget your layers for cooler mornings and evenings!                                                   │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Attractions and Cultural Events**                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  1. **The Prado Museum**: A must-visit art museum featuring an extensive collection of European art,          │
│  including works by Goya, Velázquez, and El Greco.                                                            │
│  2. **Royal Palace of Madrid**: An impressive palace that was the primary residence of Spanish monarchs for   │
│  over 300 years. Take a guided tour to explore its grand halls, chapels, and gardens.                         │
│  3. **Almudena Cathedral**: A beautiful Catholic cathedral located next to the Royal Palace, offering         │
│  stunning views of the city from its terraces.                                                                │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Hidden Gems**                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                               │
│  1. **Plaza del Mercado de San Miguel**: A charming square in the heart of Madrid, offering a variety of      │
│  food stalls, bars, and restaurants.                                                                          │
│  2. **Museo del Ferrocarril**: A small museum showcasing an impressive collection of trains, locomotives,     │
│  and railway artifacts.                                                                                       │
│  3. **Retiro Park**: A tranquil oasis in the city, perfect for a leisurely stroll or boat ride on its lake.   │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Seasonal Offerings**                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                               │
│  1. **Madrid Festival**: While it takes place in February, this festival typically occurs later in the        │
│  month, so you might miss it. However, you can still enjoy the city's vibrant cultural scene.                 │
│  2. **Flamenco Shows**: Experience the passionate and energetic rhythms of Spanish flamenco music at one of   │
│  many tablaos (flamenco bars) throughout the city.                                                            │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Daily Activity Recommendations**                                                                           │
│                                                                                                               │
│  1. Explore the historic center, including the Puerta del Sol, Plaza Mayor, and the Royal Palace.             │
│  2. Visit the Prado Museum or the Reina Sofia Museum to indulge in world-class art.                           │
│  3. Wander through Retiro Park or take a stroll along the Manzanares River.                                   │
│  4. Sample local cuisine, such as tapas, gazpacho, and jamón ibérico.                                         │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Practical Travel Tips**                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                               │
│  1. **Getting Around**: Madrid has an excellent metro system and numerous bus routes. Consider purchasing a   │
│  tourist card for convenient travel.                                                                          │
│  2. **Accommodation**: Choose a centrally located hotel or Airbnb to minimize travel time.                    │
│  3. **Language**: While many Madrileños speak English, it's always helpful to learn basic Spanish phrases,    │
│  such as "gracias" (thank you) and "¿dónde está...?" (where is...?).                                          │
│  4. **Budgeting**: Madrid can be expensive, so plan your budget accordingly, especially for food and drink.   │
│                                                                                                               │
│  **Costs**                                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                               │
│  1. **Flights**: Round-trip flights from Vienna to Madrid on February 14th, 2026, will cost approximately     │
│  €250.                                                                                                        │
│  2. **Accommodation**: Budget-friendly options start at around €40 per night for a shared room or Airbnb      │
│  apartment.                                                                                                   │
│  3. **Food**: Tapas and snacks begin at €5-€10 per person. Mid-range restaurants offer meals from €15-€25     │
│  per person.                                                                                                  │
